  "mathematical_claims": [
    "The five-moment endpoint cross polynomial has the exact rank-one birth increment p_(N+1)-p_N=8*mu(N+1)*((N+1)^(-1/2)-x)*(A_N-M_N*x).",
    "At integer births the pickup equals twice the Stieltjes prefix Q_n=sum_(k<n) M_k*(k^(-1/2)-(k+1)^(-1/2)).",
    "For P_K=sum_(n<K) log((n+1)/n)*(Q_n^2+Q_(n+1)^2) and V_K=sum_(n<K) log((n+1)/n)*x_n^2, P_K-4V_K<=H(log K)<=4P_K.",
    "The weighted variation satisfies V_K<=1/2 by coefficient magnitude and elementary telescoping.",
    "Therefore P_K-2<=H(log K)<=4P_K, and a dyadic all-positive-rate P_K bound is equivalent to the complete endpoint estimate.",
    "Increment square mass alone cannot control the Hardy-prefix mass; normalized flat finite packets have square mass one and Hardy mass (L+1)/2."
  ],
